# The one copairing of the sum `Fit | Failed`: `describe` takes it and tests it once; each arm gives back an object
# literal of the interface Report, which its return type names, so each arm builds a Report (`return { .. }`), and the
# route gives the Report either arm built. The early return is the one arm, what follows it the other.

route fits.report.describe
choice describe/?1
step describe/?1/Report()                                         # `return { line: .., points: [r.score] }`
step describe/?1/Report()#2                            # what follows the early return is the other arm

line entry > describe call
known #127 line Fit | Failed·r > describe value                    # the route's parameter, by its name
known #127 line Fit | Failed·r > describe/?1/Report() value        # `r.score`
known #127 line Fit | Failed·r > describe/?1/Report()#2 value      # `r.reason`
line describe/?1/Report() > Report@describe/?1 value   # with the other arm's Report, the value either arm makes
line describe/?1/Report()#2 > Report@describe/?1 value
line Report@describe/?1 > describe value
line describe > Report@describe value                             # the result goes on to the caller

known #127 home Fit | Failed·r describe
home Report@describe/?1 describe
home Report@describe describe

side entry left

# a parameter whose type is a sum written in place keeps no name, and is taken as one of its variants
known #127 extra line Fit | Failed > describe value
known #127 extra home Fit | Failed describe

# the route's parameter is taken as the variant its type names first, by its name
known #127 extra line Fit·r > describe/?1/Report() value
known #127 extra line Fit·r > describe/?1/Report()#2 value
known #127 extra home Fit·r describe/?1
